{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/pulls/998","id":4251459541,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSbOoU879aB_V","html_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/998","diff_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/998.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/pull/998.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/998","number":998,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Repair reported dialog and reporting regressions","user":{"login":"konard","id":1431904,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzE5MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1431904?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard","html_url":"https://github.com/konard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\n- keep current-location questions, Links Notation definitions, British `behaviour` queries, conversation preferences/corrections, associative-memory inspection, and explicit unquoted teaching rules on their intended local routes\n- mirror the new dialog and memory behavior in the browser worker while preventing ordinary file edits from being misclassified as behavior-rule declarations\n- retain failed search/fetch diagnostics instead of rendering an empty successful research result\n- add `formal-ai report body --separate-context-links`, which exports and uploads harness, server, and merged context independently with safe filenames and valid link-only Markdown\n- preserve the complete reported dialog, requirements mapping, red/green evidence, and a reproducible Formal AI / Agent CLI self-authorship proof\n\nFixes https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/issues/989\n\n## Root causes and reproducing tests\n\n| Reported family | Root cause and fix | Regression |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Local routing | Missing seeded location/control/memory cues and agentic precedence let generic web/document plans capture local turns. Added seed-backed handlers and moved memory inspection before agentic planning. | `tests/unit/issue_989.rs` whole-dialog, location, conversation-control, and memory tests |\n| Links Notation definition | The formalization recipe treated the output-format noun as an action. It now requires a seeded formalization verb. | `links_notation_question_falls_through_to_the_symbolic_concept_answer` |\n| Web transport failure | Planners checked completed capability state without checking its latest failed observation, while status-less inference scanned arbitrary successful page contents. Planners now terminate with stored diagnostics and prose inference is limited to the leading diagnostic region. | `failed_web_transport_is_reported_as_failure_not_empty_success`, `successful_web_page_with_record_404_is_not_a_transport_failure` |\n| Teaching and behaviour rules | The compiler required backtick pairs, and recursive role evidence made generic action words too broad. Added seed-driven unquoted parsing and direct-role matching in Rust/JS, plus British aliases. | `plain_text_trigger_and_answer_compile_and_replay`, `ordinary_file_edits_are_not_mistaken_for_dialog_control`, browser mirror |\n| Issue reports | One merged attachment could not produce the three requested links. The CLI now performs three independent gist uploads, suppresses empty fences for link-only attachments, and sanitizes session-derived context filenames. | issue-989 unit tests plus real CLI integrations for three-link reporting and temp-directory path containment in `tests/integration/issue_822_context.rs` |\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test --test unit issue_989 -- --nocapture` — 14 passed\n- `cargo test --test source -- --nocapture` — 487 passed, including the macOS-timeout test locally in 2.34s\n- `cargo test --test integration -- --nocapture` — 333 passed, 1 ignored; includes real-CLI path containment for a malicious session name\n- full unit matrix — 2,656 passed before two stale derived-evidence assertions; the refreshed Agent-authored fixture and both evidence assertions then passed in focused reruns (9/9)\n- `PORT=8894 experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_771.sh` — passed; three context gists linked and report body verified\n- `PORT=8896 experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_822.sh` — passed; both confirmations precede three independently verified context links\n- `PORT=8899 ARTIFACT_DIR=/tmp/issue989-issue819-green experiments/agent_cli_e2e/run_issue_819_report_tui.sh` — passed; real TUI selection flow and all three linked files verified\n- `bun test` in `experiments/agent_cli_e2e/issue_819_tui` — 4 passed\n- `node --test tests/web/worker-mirror.test.mjs` — 15 passed\n- `npm run test:web` — passed\n- `cargo clippy --lib --bins --tests --all-features -- -D warnings` — passed\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — passed\n- `cargo test --doc --verbose` — passed\n- `python3 scripts/audit-total-closure.py .` — 0 unresolved tokens across 4,151 value tokens\n- seed metadata and minimal-core audits — 3,513 recorded gaps and 19,711 outside-core lines, both current\n- `npm run --prefix tests/e2e check:language-parity` — passed, including Spanish coverage for each changed response family\n- self-AST census — 10 passed; regenerated snapshots match source\n- neighboring memory, reporting, formalization, seed/fragment, minimal-core, worker-budget, coverage-ratchet, docs, examples, rustdoc, docs.rs, WASM, and size/policy checks — passed\n- `cargo test --all-features` passed the implementation/integration suites; one host disk-free sampling assertion in issue-752 drifted during the broad run and passed immediately in its isolated suite rerun\n- post-`origin/main` check: focused Rust 14/14, source 487/487, integration 333/333, browser 15/15, language parity, five-language regression coverage, and all three real Agent CLI/TUI reporting flows passed on head `18ae70c7`\n\n## Evidence and self-application\n\nThe [issue #989 case study](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-989-66076bee90a1/docs/case-studies/issue-989/README.md) retains the byte-identical 1,438-line report, research, root-cause analysis, requirement-to-test matrix, and red/green logs. The [PR case study](https://github.com/link-assistant/formal-ai/blob/issue-989-66076bee90a1/docs/case-studies/pull-request-998/README.md) records review decisions and the initial state of all three PR discussion surfaces.\n\nA live external Agent CLI backed by the locally built Formal AI server authored one reviewed smallest leaf in session `ses_00fc002c9ffetId67J25NEeudn`. The decomposition has five leaves, so the byte-pinned Formal AI-authored leaf is 20% of the task; its artifact and server/client logs are retained under `docs/case-studies/issue-989/self-hosting-authorship/`.\n\nThe same external-CLI harness refreshed the planner-derived self-healing fixture in session `ses_00ea26880ffeRCSs97U7BNbw9A`; the emitted artifact, server trace, and client trace are retained byte-for-byte under `docs/case-studies/issue-905/self-hosting-fixture-refresh/`.\n\nNo visual UI changed, so screenshots and visual regression tests are not applicable. No dependency or third-party source material was added.\n","created_at":"2026-08-11T08:23:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-11T16:26:07Z","closed_at":"2026-08-11T16:26:05Z","merged_at":"2026-08-11T16:26:05Z","merge_commit_sha":"d00c61686d0a51c9932558f4be858e5a5febe153","assignees":[{"logi